<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank won't comment on Natwest bid talk.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank won't comment on Natwest bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerzbank AG on Tuesday declined to comment on market rumours that it may be a bidder for Britain's National Westminster Bank whose shares hit a record high on market talk of an imminent takeover bid.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't comment on speculation,&quot; a Commerzbank spokesman said in response to a Reuter enquiry.</p>
<p>But banking sources ruled out the possibility of a bid by Commerzbank.</p>
<p>NatWest shares jumped to a record high of 858 pence on Tuesday, up from Monday's close of 807.5 pence, on talk of a possible bidder which focused on Barclays Plc as well as on Commerzbank.</p>
<p>The shares fell to 843 pence in late trade.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
